          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_2.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{PD}}{\\mathrm{BD}} = \\tan 30^{\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\quad  or  \\quad \\mathrm{BD} = \\mathrm{PD} \\sqrt{3}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.199,
            0.351,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In right "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\; \\mathrm { P A C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.231,
            0.51,
            0.272
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{PC}{AC} = \\tan 45^{\\circ} = 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.283,
            0.142,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.307,
            0.155,
            0.325
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.326,
            0.281,
            0.772,
            0.326
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} & PC  =  AC  \\\\& PC  =  PD  +  DC ,  therefore ,  PD  +  DC  =  AC .\\\\ \\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.338,
            0.873,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A C } = \\mathrm { B D }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{DC} = \\mathrm{AB} = 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " m, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "PD + 8 = BD = PD\\sqrt{3} (\\text{Why?})"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.398,
            0.206,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This gives"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.326,
            0.375,
            0.829,
            0.436
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{PD} = \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3} - 1} = \\frac{8\\left( \\sqrt{3} + 1 \\right)}{\\left( \\sqrt{3} + 1 \\right)\\left( \\sqrt{3} - 1 \\right)} = 4\\left( \\sqrt{3} + 1 \\right)\\mathrm{m}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.443,
            0.895,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { S o } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the height of the multi-storeyed building is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left\\{ 4\\left( \\sqrt{3} + 1 \\right) + 8 \\right\\} = 4\\left( 3 + \\sqrt{3} \\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " m and the distance between the two buildings is also "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4(3 + \\sqrt{3})  m"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.517,
            0.902,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 7 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " From a point on a bridge across a river, the angles of depression of the banks on opposite sides of the river are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , respectively. If the bridge is at a height of 3 m from the banks, find the width of the river."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.58,
            0.422,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In Fig 9.10, A and B represent points on the bank on opposite sides of the river, so that AB is the width of the river. P is a point on the bridge at a height of 3 m , i . e . , "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { D P } = 3 \\mathrm { ~ m } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We are interested to determine the width of the river, which is the length of the side AB of the D APB."
            }
          ]
        },
